  * its CS words: REQ_RESOURCE compute, the compute staging registers (SRT r0, FAU r8, SPD r16, TSD
  * r24, WG_SIZE r33, JOB_SIZE r37-r39), RUN_COMPUTE, WAIT, FLUSH_CACHE2, WAIT.
  *   mul_add (0098): out[i] = in[i] * MUL + ADD. Boot 0098 ran it on the cores (no fault, 210 us) but
- *     every result was in[i] + ADD: the IMUL product never reached the IADD.
+ *     every result was in[i] + ADD: the IMUL product never reached the IADD. Cause (found by the
+ *     probe in 0099): a .waitN takes effect after its instruction, and mul_add had the wait on the
+ *     IMUL itself, so the IMUL read r4 before the LOAD landed. 0100 moves it one instruction up.
  *   imul_probe (0099): five variants of that arithmetic, one 1 KiB output array each (see
  *     tools/gpu/imul_probe.vhasm), to tell an IMUL, FAU-operand, register or ordering fault apart.
  * The shader cores' domain (pd_embedded_g3d) is on from ABL; CSF firmware powers the cores.
